# The Windows install guide has students set git to "checkout Windows-style, commit
# Unix-style", so without these every one of these files arrives on a Windows machine
# with CRLF line endings. bash then fails on the shebang with "$'\r': command not
# found" and GNU make appends a carriage return to every argument in a recipe. Neither
# error mentions line endings and both get reported as "the repo is broken".
*.sh     text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.qmd    text eol=lf
*.Rmd    text eol=lf
*.ipynb  text eol=lf
